 <comment>A sliding puzzle of three layers, after Goh Pit Khiam&apos;s Number Blocks. Each block is a 2 by 2 plate below and above, joined by a hollow middle layer with nubs that stick out sideways. The frame has a 6 by 6 window below and above and an 8 by 8 gap between them, under its ring. A nub may pass under another block&apos;s top plate, but not through its core or its nubs. Bring the blocks into reading order, 1 to 8, the gap bottom right: 104 moves at the fewest. Generated by search (design 118).</comment>
</puzzle>
